<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>RMS Book - Ch1Q2 - Interpreting varietal response</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Mission 2: Let the evidence challenge your question</h3><p>The following are <strong>simulated mean yields</strong> (tonnes per hectare) from an illustrative trial. They are not observations from the chapter.</p><table border="1" cellpadding="6"><tr><th>Irrigation</th><th>Variety A</th><th>Variety B</th></tr><tr><td>Low</td><td>{@aL/10@}</td><td>{@bL/10@}</td></tr><tr><td>Medium</td><td>{@aM/10@}</td><td>{@bM/10@}</td></tr><tr><td>High</td><td>{@aH/10@}</td><td>{@bH/10@}</td></tr></table><p>1. Calculate B minus A at <strong>low</strong> irrigation (t/ha): [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>2. Calculate B minus A at <strong>high</strong> irrigation (t/ha): [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>3. Calculate (B minus A at high irrigation) minus (B minus A at low irrigation): [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</p><p><strong>Decision checkpoint:</strong> What do the calculated contrasts suggest?</p><p>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</p>
[[hint title="Hint: compare contrasts"]]<p>A difference-in-differences of zero means the two endpoint contrasts agree; a positive or negative value means the contrast has changed.</p>[[/hint]]
<p><em>These are simulated means. An apparent interaction is not a statistical significance test.</em></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>At low irrigation, B minus A is {@ta1@} t/ha. At high irrigation, B minus A is {@ta2@} t/ha. Their difference is {@ta3@} t/ha.</p>
[[if test="is(pattern=0)"]]<p>The variety advantage is constant across the two endpoints. These means do not show a change in the varietal contrast between low and high irrigation.</p>
[[elif test="is(pattern=1)"]]<p>The preferred variety reverses: B leads at low irrigation, while A leads at high irrigation.</p>
[[else]]<p>B leads at both irrigation levels, but the size of its advantage changes. That is an interaction in the observed means.</p>[[/if]]
<p>To assess whether a population-level interaction is supported, we would need information on replication and variability and an appropriate analysis.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
